theta = 0.55, C_dyn = 300000, k5 = pss, chemistry netmodernli, equilibrium table where p ≥ 1e+30, AV ql1 = 0.15 cq2 = 1, central t_ff0 = 4.892e+04 yr
   step  log n_c     t [yr]       T_c  ON98 T_c     f_H2,c u_c [km/s]  max dT/T    dt [s]
STARLIGHT: three-level H (Peebles C factor, Sobolev Lya escape, e collisions) in the lit network zones
LYABB: three-level H bound-bound (Lya pumping / collisional de-excitation, collisional excitation / Lya + 2-photon escape) heat in the chemistry
NLOPACJ: kappa_E of network zones weighted with the star light's B_nu(T_c)
SLEB: star-light colour temperature T_r at tau + 2/3 (Eddington-Barbier), not the photosphere's T_eff
SLBLEND: star-light colour temperature T_eff (tau <= 0.3) to T_r (tau >= 3), smooth in log tau
PSWSTAY=0: below the pressure switch a table zone stays on the table only by the tau rule
NLOPAC: non-LTE opacity in the three-level network zones (no H bound-free in kappa_P; n=2 of the three-level atom in kappa_R)
NLOIT: network-zone opacities from the Newton iterate's own populations (table x continuum-code ratio at the iterate; NLOIMPT, NLODAMP, CPLNLOX, NLOFIX, NLOTMAX inactive there)
STARLIGHT: H- detachment, LW (shield sobolev) from the star's light in network zones
LINEIMP: H2 line cooling of each zone from its own state (populations at the iterate's T, radiative rates of the last transfer call); no t_cool cap, no IMPCOOL slope
HOT: stellar branch above T1 = 3e+05 K (full at 9e+05 K), Delta0 = 1.0920e+13 erg/g, D/H = 2.50e-05
restarted from checkpoint z19zie1S16 at step 63334, t = 2.773335e+05 yr, log n_c = 24.229, T_c = 142281187.2 K
NKRYLOV: Newton corrections by GMRES on the true Jacobian (eta 0.001, Krylov dimension 30, eps 1e-05), band Jacobian as preconditioner
SLABFLUX: interface opacity from the steady slab solution, profile kappa ~ (tau + tau0)^n, n = Inf (exponential in tau)
SLABTIE: FLUXTIE outward donor h = h_FS + f/(tau_i + 2f) - f/(a + 2f), tau_i the slab depth of the donor centre below the interface, a its half-zone depth
ECOMPAT: TIEFRAME switched on
ECOMPAT: first-law gas row adjoint to the momentum row in every zone, lab-frame radiation energy row
FLUXTIE: radiation momentum row -> F = h c E (h = H/J of the formal solution) where tau from the outer boundary <= 0.1, blended to the moment equation by tau = 1
VEFIMP=1: Eddington factors f, g and the flux tie's h of the formal solution at every Newton iterate (not lagged); radiation momentum row and outer boundary in Auer's sphericality-factor form (exact for chi = 0); the CMB only as the isotropic background, added to the formal solution's moments analytically
SLIMP: star light of the coupled zones at the Newton iterate: dilution W, colour temperature, Lyman-Werner shielding, Lyα escape (local variables of the zone's chemistry and NLOIT opacity)
COUPLED: x_H+ and x_H2 of the network zones are unknowns 8 and 9 of the hydro Newton (neqn 9, meqn 9)
ETOTMON: total-energy rows of every converged solve (TX.etot_monitor) -> ETOT text on the DTERR trace lines, etot_* columns of perf.csv
DTERR: error-controlled TR-BDF2 (rtol 0.03, conv 0.01, x floor 1e-06, F floor 1 cE, E floor 0 aT^4, rms norm, PI true, safety/facmin/facmax 0.9/0.2/5, Newton-failure factor 0.25, BE retry false); TITAN's heuristic and caps are diagnostic only
